critic_gaps.what:
This freeze audit ran the pinned prompt with its pre-launch scope and context lines unchanged. round1_pinned_procedure.js:11 still reads 'Code under review = git diff f7fe73b..HEAD', and line 12 still reads 'Context: no v5 calibration has run yet; this review is the pre-launch checkpoint'. The checkpoint record says otherwise (metanet_v5_code_review.md:3): 'For an audit, the prompt's scope line names the diff from the last reviewed commit and the outputs under audit'. As a result:
- no lens was pointed at the committed STOP record (5a733be), freeze_stops.json or cma_summary.json;
- line 13 ('NEVER simulate a real calibration day with a candidate plant') stopped anyone reproducing the recorded verdict;
- the unchanged imported modules that §B11.2 item 3 puts in audit scope (metanet_events/inputs/facts, corridor_analysis, mndot) were outside every lens's diff.
My own check was read-only, with no simulation, and found the record consistent with the code:
- cma_restart_7192011 best_x equals nominal_x, and the facts sha matches;
- freeze_stops 'code' and cma_summary code_commit are both 3d4402f, the last CODE_PATHS commit. The only CODE_PATHS change after the checkpoint's fix commit d64b3f7 is the facts commit;
- the screen used the P8 tolerance 3 and Lc_k equal to F8 ci_r[0] (0.99397 and 0.92609); no real-data minimum was unmet (n_A 22/9, n_H 22/9, n_H_first 22); need() gives 17 and 7;
- every failed row is beyond its §5.3 threshold: P3-1 16/22 = 0.727 < 0.75; P4-1 matched share 0.654; P5a-1 15 < 17 matched; P6-1 upper half |8 − 11| = 3 > k = 2; P7b 3/22; P1c CI upper bound 0.26 > 0;
- the nominal J5 rows agree with the gate: P3-1 0.289 equals 6 misses with mean s ≈ 0.12; P7b 0.862 against a gate hit share of 0.136; P8g 0, because the one B1 extra falls on a miss day.

Neither metanet_v5_gate.verdict() (lines 290-304) nor metanet_v5_freeze.finalize() (lines 407-473) contains any logic or field for the labels the protocol requires:
- 'second look on the same validation days' (KILL-only) for any post-look FAIL → PASS;
- 'after post-result fix' with both outcomes, for a fix that leaves the outcome unchanged or changes only the nominal or the members;
- the 'Disclosed' citation of the original outcome when a fix reverses a pre-look stop ('Every later result cites both outcomes').
After a fix re-run, verdict() returns a bare 'PASS' or 'PASS, substitute spread'. Nothing reads the fix records except the guard. No test covers these labels; test 36 covers only the guard.

A §B11.2 full re-run on the original seeds destroys the original outcome's raw data:
- _batch unlinks cma_restart_{s}.json (metanet_v5_calibrate.py:310-311);
- restart() overwrites cma_state_{s}.pkl (line 227);
- run() overwrites cma_base_summary.json and cma_summary.json (lines 365, 385);
- freeze_stops() overwrites freeze_stops.json (metanet_v5_freeze.py:393);
- grid_run unlinks the grid files (lines 598-599).
The committed record keeps only the nominal's x: its restarts list omits best_x and best_rows (lines 414-416). The gate path, by contrast, archives superseded draws (metanet_v5_gate.py:325-330).
The re-run is also not guarded:
- run() does not require a committed fix record before re-running seeds 7,192,010-017. §B11.2 item 1 says the record is 'committed with the test below, before the re-run', but the only fix-record check sits at the gate;
- fix_record_valid (metanet_v5_gate.py:88-94) only checks that the named test path exists at the fix commit, not that it 'fails on the code that produced the result';
- run() refuses to launch whenever the facts hash changed since the premise check (line 355). A facts-code fix therefore forces a premise re-run, although §B11.2 says 'The premise check is repeated only to confirm a fix to its own anchor'.

